<p class="lt-chem-335305">What is the concentration of As(III) in a sample of water if its peak current is 1.37 &mu;A?</p>

<div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/Analytical_Chemistry/Instrumental_Analysis_(LibreTexts)/25:_Voltammetry/25.07:_Voltammetry_with_Ultramicroelectrodes" class="mt-section"><span id="Solution"></span><h6 class="lt-chem-335305 editable">Solution</h6>

<p class="lt-chem-335305">Linear regression gives the calibration curve shown in Figure \(\PageIndex{1}\), with an equation of</p>

<p class="lt-chem-335305">\[i_{p}=0.0176+3.01 \times[\mathrm{As}(\mathrm{III})] \nonumber \]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-335305">Substituting the sample&rsquo;s peak current into the regression equation gives the concentration of As(III) as 4.49 &mu;M.</p>
</div></div></section>

